```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n", composed.date);
        if !composed.overview.is_empty() {
            message.push_str(&composed.overview);
            message.push('\n');
        }
        for entry in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str(&format!(
                "- {} ({}) {}\n",
                entry.title, entry.feed, entry.link
            ));
        }

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out both of the operations requests. This node is granted only `Notifier<'digest'>`, and the crate has no filesystem import. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a new log capability that the graph would have to declare. The metadata fetch would need an `http-client` import scoped to that host, and it would also send the digest text to an external service that this node has not been granted. Both would widen the node's authority beyond its contract. If operations wants either one, it should be added as a declared capability in the graph, with its allowlist and scope reviewed first.

